---
const steps = [
  {
    name: "How I show up in a team",
    brief: [
      "Marketing rarely happens in isolation. Most of the work happens in conversations — often unstructured, sometimes unclear.",
      "I tend to <strong>bring structure into vague discussions</strong>. Not by forcing answers too quickly, but by asking the questions that make things clearer: what are we actually trying to solve, what doesn’t make sense yet, where are we making assumptions?",
      "I <strong>challenge ideas without shutting them down</strong>. Because strong work usually comes from refining something — not replacing it entirely.",
      "At the same time, I try to create an environment where <strong>ideas can be explored without pressure</strong>. Where thoughts don’t have to be fully formed to be useful.",
      "And in many cases, I naturally take the role of <strong>shaping the narrative</strong> — connecting inputs, structuring arguments, and turning scattered ideas into something coherent."
    ]
  },
  {
    name: "From messy ideas to a clear story",
    brief: [
      "Most ideas don’t start as clear arguments.",
      "They start fragmented — half-formed thoughts, different opinions, loose directions that don’t fully connect yet.",
      "A big part of my role is to <strong>find the thread that runs through all of it</strong>. Not by forcing a narrative too early, but by <strong>questioning what actually holds up</strong> and what doesn’t.",
      "I look for where things feel off — where arguments contradict each other, where something sounds right but doesn’t fully make sense yet. Because clarity usually doesn’t come from adding more. It comes from <strong>removing what doesn’t belong</strong>.",
      "From there, I structure ideas in a way that works on two levels: <strong>logically</strong> — so it can be followed, and <strong>emotionally</strong> — so it actually resonates.",
      "Presentations are not just about making things look good. They are about making something <strong>clear enough that people can move forward with it</strong>."
    ]
  },
  {
    name: "Behind the final slide",
    brief: [
      "The final output often looks clean and obvious. But getting there is rarely linear.",
      "It involves <strong>structuring discussions</strong> that don’t yet have a clear direction.<br/><strong>Building a storyline</strong> that holds together from beginning to end.<br/><strong>Sharpening arguments</strong> until they feel precise, not just plausible.<br/>And finding the right <strong>tone</strong> — so that something is not only correct, but actually resonates.",
      "A big part of the work is making complexity <strong>feel simple without oversimplifying it</strong>.",
      "Because when something finally “clicks”, it usually doesn’t mean it became easier.",
      "It means it became <strong>clear enough to move forward</strong>."
    ]
  }
];
---
<section id="process" class="process-section editorial-section">
  <div class="process-spread reveal">
    <div class="editorial-list">
      {steps.map((step, index) => (
        <div class={`step-item reveal delay-${index + 1}`}>
          <div class="step-number">0{index + 1}.</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h4 class="step-name">{step.name}</h4>
            <div class="step-description">
              {step.brief.map(paragraph => (
                <p class="step-brief" set:html={paragraph} />
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="process-header">
      <div class="chapter-meta">me as a team member</div>
      <h3 class="process-title">
        <span class="thinking-text">what makes the</span>
        <span class="work-text">difference</span>
      </h3>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .process-spread {
    padding: 100px 5vw;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; /* Matching Case Studies ratio */
    gap: 100px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    max-width: 1600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .process-header {
    position: sticky;
    top: 150px;
    text-align: right;
    padding-right: 2vw; /* Matching Case Studies offset */
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-end;
  }

  .chapter-meta {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    text-transform: lowercase;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.4em;
    color: var(--text-main);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .process-title {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 6.5vw, 7.5rem);
    line-height: 0.9;
    color: var(--text-main);
    text-transform: lowercase;
    letter-spacing: -0.06em;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .thinking-text {
    display: block;
  }

  .work-text {
    display: block;
    font-family: 'Amsterdam Four', cursive;
    color: var(--accent-color);
    font-weight: 100;
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    margin-top: -0.45em; /* Increased overlap */
    margin-left: 1.5rem; /* Pushed more to the right */
    transform: rotate(-8.5deg);
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    opacity: 0.85;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .editorial-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--text-main);
  }

  .step-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 60px;
    padding: 60px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
  }

  .step-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--text-main);
  }

  .step-number {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    padding-top: 15px;
  }

  .step-content {
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  .step-name {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    text-transform: lowercase; /* Matches About and Approach titles */
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .step-brief {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-main);
    max-width: 500px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .step-brief:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .delay-1 { transition-delay: 0.1s; }
  .delay-2 { transition-delay: 0.2s; }
  .delay-3 { transition-delay: 0.3s; }

  @media (max-width: 968px) {
    .process-spread { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 60px; }
    .process-header { position: static; }
    .step-item { flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; padding: 40px 0; }
    .step-number { padding-top: 0; }
  }
</style>
